# Email transport providers

Transactional and marketing email go through a **provider registry** (same pattern as alerting / payments). Built-ins: Resend (default), SendGrid, Amazon SES. Plugins can register additional transports.

Relevant modules: [app/libs/email/index.server.js](mdc:app/libs/email/index.server.js), [app/libs/email-types.server.js](mdc:app/libs/email-types.server.js), adapters under [app/libs/email/](mdc:app/libs/email/), templates/send helpers in [app/emails/index.server.jsx](mdc:app/emails/index.server.jsx).

## What to call

| Use case | Import | Notes |
| ----- | --- | ----- |
| Send a named template | `sendWelcomeEmail`, `sendOrderConfirmationEmail`, … from `#/emails/index.server` | Renders React Email → HTML, then active provider |
| Raw HTML send | `sendEmail` from `#/libs/email/index.server` | Low-level; pass `{ from, to, subject, html }` |
| Custom / plugin provider | `registerProvider` from `#/libs/email/index.server` or `defineProvider('email', …)` | Plugin enable wires registration |

Do **not** import `resend` (or other ESP SDKs) from app code outside `#/libs/email/*`.

## Configuration

From [`.env.example`](mdc:.env.example):

- `EMAIL_PROVIDER` — fallback provider id when the `email.provider` setting is unset (default: `resend`)
- `RESEND_API_KEY` — Resend
- `SENDGRID_API_KEY` — SendGrid
- `SES_REGION` / `SES_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `SES_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` — Amazon SES (falls back to `AWS_REGION` / `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`)

Merchants can also choose the provider in **Admin → Settings → Email** (`SETTING_KEYS.EMAIL_PROVIDER`).

## Custom providers (plugins)

```js
import { definePlugin, defineProvider } from '#/core/plugins/index.server';

export const pluginManifest = definePlugin({
  providers: {
    postmark: defineProvider('email', {
      name: 'Postmark',
      async send({ from, to, subject, html, text }) {
        return { success: true };
      },
    }),
  },
});
```

Enable the plugin, then select it under Settings → Email.
